Bilkul. Agar tumhe kisi aur component ya backend se data lena ho, to aksar ngOnInit() ek achhi jagah hoti hai.

Example 1: Backend se data lena
ngOnInit() {
  this.userService.getUsers().subscribe(data => {
    this.users = data;
  });
}

Jab component load hoga, API call chalegi aur data aa jayega.

Example 2: Parent component se data lena

Parent HTML:

<app-child [customer]="selectedCustomer"></app-child>

Child component:

@Input() customer: any;

ngOnInit() {
  console.log(this.customer);
}

Note: Agar customer baad me change ho sakta hai, to ngOnChanges() zyada suitable hota hai.

Example 3: Service se data lena
constructor(private authService: AuthService) {}

ngOnInit() {
  this.user = this.authService.getCurrentUser();
}
Simple rule

ngOnInit() tab use karo jab component load hote hi:

✅ API se data lena ho
✅ Service se data lena ho
✅ Initial setup karna ho
✅ Default values set karni ho
✅ Listener start karna ho
